{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"gnatty-comparable-ynambu","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem (parity siblings of the tickets-branch invariant violation)\nTwo more tickets-branch writers bypass the shared store seams and the two-part invariant\n(under the unified write lock + auto-commit/publish), same class as projects_store\n(ticket fea4-f98c-f1a2-4168):\n1. reconcile_helpers._commit_binding_store_snapshot (reconcile_helpers.py:169) commits\n   .bridge_state binding/rotation/link state via raw git_adapter.add + commit. git_adapter\n   imports only rebar._store.gitutil.run_git — it does NOT acquire rebar._store.lock.write_lock,\n   so it races the ticket-CLI _push_tickets_branch() and any concurrent GHA commit-back\n   (the exact class of race the write lock exists to prevent). Its own docstring documents\n   the \"un-committed local copy silently overwritten by a concurrent run\" bug it half-fixes\n   WITHOUT taking the lock.\n2. alert_store._atomic_write (alert_store.py:84) hand-rolls tempfile+os.replace instead of\n   the shared rebar._store.fsutil.atomic_write seam.\n\n## Approach\n1. Migrate _commit_binding_store_snapshot to commit its (already-computed) file list\n   through the shared locked commit+push facade introduced in ticket fea4\n   (write_lock -> rebase guard -> _git_commit_paths -> push_tickets_branch), removing the\n   lock-bypassing raw git_adapter add/commit. Preserve its EXACT current file set\n   (BINDINGS/RETIRED/GET_ROTATION/IMPOSSIBLE_LINKS/PEER_CONFIRMATIONS), its per-file\n   idempotency (bug 1e08), and its fail-open posture (a commit failure must still NOT\n   abort the pass — the facade's StoreError is caught and logged, returning False as today).\n2. Replace alert_store._atomic_write with fsutil.atomic_write. FIRST determine whether\n   bridge_alerts files are committed to the tickets branch (GHA commit-back / any git add)\n   or are local-only scratch: if committed, route through the locked facade too; if local\n   scratch, fsutil.atomic_write alone is sufficient (no lock). Document the finding.\n\n## Constraints — BEHAVIOR-PRESERVING\nVerify the migration changes NO functionality: same files staged, same idempotent no-op\nwhen nothing changed, same graceful-degradation on git error, same serialized bytes for\nalert files. Add tests that pin these before/after.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. _commit_binding_store_snapshot serializes through write_lock (assert the lock is\n   acquired) and commits via _git_commit_paths + push; behavior otherwise identical\n   (same file set, idempotency, fail-open).\n2. alert_store uses fsutil.atomic_write; residency (committed vs scratch) determined and\n   the correct seam (locked facade vs atomic_write only) applied + documented.\n3. No functional/behavioral change beyond the lock+seam adoption (pinned by tests).\n\n## Sequencing\nDepends on ticket fea4 (provides the shared locked commit+push facade). Edits\nreconcile_helpers.py + alert_store.py (+ tests) — disjoint from A/C/D. Start AFTER fea4\nlands (rebase onto it).","id":"6454-d06e-7361-4e3d","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Parity: migrate binding-store snapshot + alert_store onto shared locked commit+push / atomic_write seams (behavior-preserving)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786807671442401001,"uuid":"fdd18f49-57b4-4c8f-ae16-6063b343e978"}